 "instructions": "# Task (round 4): official APPLICATION FEE for the remaining schools\n\nGoal: for each item in \"tasks\" (school + level bachelor/master) find the official application fee for international applicants, using the school's OFFICIAL website only.\nlast_url / last_status show what happened in the previous round (blocked, not_found, js_empty, read).\n\nMethod\n- Browse like a person: real browser, normal pace (a few seconds between page loads), one page at a time.\n- Wait for pages and automatic browser checks to finish loading; expand accordions, tabs and \"show more\" panels; read hidden text.\n- Look in: \"Tuition & fees\", \"Fees and costs\", \"Cost of attendance\", \"How to apply\", \"Apply\", \"International admissions\", \"Admissions FAQ\", fee schedules as PDF/spreadsheet on the school's own site, programme pages, and country selectors (choose Turkey or \"international / non-EU\", then the right level).\n- Search the school's own site: site:<school-domain> \"application fee\".\n- Official domains only. No agent, aggregator or forum sites.\n- If a page asks you to solve a CAPTCHA or otherwise blocks automated access, do not try to get around it. Set page_status \"blocked\", put the exact URL in manual_check_url so a person can open it, and continue with other official pages of that school.\n- Also record the admissions office contact email or contact-form URL from the official site in contact (so a person can ask about the fee).\n- An application fee is the fee paid when submitting the application. Not tuition, deposit, registration, enrolment, test or visa fees. Write \"none\" only if an official page explicitly says there is no application fee (quote it in application_fee_note). Otherwise null. Never guess or infer.\n- For UK undergraduate applications through UCAS, report any fee the university itself charges (usually none) and mention in the note that UCAS charges its own fee.\n\nOutput: JSON list, one object per item, same order, no extra text:\n{\"school\",\"level\",\n \"application_fee\": \"amount with currency e.g. 'USD 75', or 'none', or null\",\n \"application_fee_note\": \"exact short quote or paraphrase from the page, plus variations (programme, country, waiver)\",\n \"source_url\": \"exact page or PDF where you read it\",\n \"manual_check_url\": \"URL a person should open when blocked, else null\",\n \"contact\": \"admissions email or contact form URL, else null\",\n \"page_status\": \"read | blocked | not_found | js_empty\",\n \"confidence\": \"high | medium | low\",\n \"english\": {\"IELTS\":null,\"TOEFL\":null,\"PTE\":null,\"Duolingo\":null}}\n\nSubmit: POST https://paneledu.com/api/agent/results with header X-Agent-Token: <token you were given>, Content-Type: application/json, body = JSON list (1-10 objects per request; send each batch as soon as it is done). Expected answer: {\"ok\":true,\"saved\":N}.\n",
